1355
01:04:41,120 --> 01:04:43,120
And bring me that cylinder.

1356
01:04:43,120 --> 01:04:46,120
And pick me up a frappuccino too.

1357
01:04:46,120 --> 01:04:49,120
Where'd you put those Christmas decorations?

1358
01:04:49,120 --> 01:04:52,120
Here's something.

1359
01:04:52,120 --> 01:04:54,120
No, that's not it either.

1360
01:04:54,120 --> 01:04:56,120
Uh-oh, does that look like the dishwasher's leaking?

1361
01:04:56,120 --> 01:04:58,120
That's hopeless, Roger.

1362
01:04:58,120 --> 01:05:00,120
Not as long as we're alive.

1363
01:05:00,120 --> 01:05:02,120
Oh, sue me.

1364
01:05:02,120 --> 01:05:08,120
Kristen McNerney looking wonderful in a Vivian Westwood.

1365
01:05:08,120 --> 01:05:09,120
He's a transvestite.

1366
01:05:09,120 --> 01:05:11,120
He likes to wear pants in private.

1367
01:05:11,120 --> 01:05:16,120
We're free.

1368
01:05:16,120 --> 01:05:19,120
It was so easy, really.

1369
01:05:19,120 --> 01:05:22,120
Well, that's another fine mess you've gotten us into, Stanley.

1370
01:05:22,120 --> 01:05:26,120
Why don't we just give up and apply for Sumerian citizenship?

1371
01:05:26,120 --> 01:05:28,120
I don't like mushrooms.

1372
01:05:28,120 --> 01:05:29,120
Oh, now, don't complain, Rog.

1373
01:05:29,120 --> 01:05:31,120
Last night we had cave rats for dinner.

1374
01:05:31,120 --> 01:05:33,120
You got cave rats.

1375
01:05:33,120 --> 01:05:35,120
Now, why don't we settle down?

1376
01:05:35,120 --> 01:05:36,120
Start a family.

1377
01:05:36,120 --> 01:05:37,120
Especially you.

1378
01:05:37,120 --> 01:05:38,120
Why, especially me?

1379
01:05:38,120 --> 01:05:40,120
Well, there's a doll.

1380
01:05:40,120 --> 01:05:43,120
Just imagine what some future archaeologist would think

1381
01:05:43,120 --> 01:05:45,120
if they happened to rediscover this world.

1382
01:05:45,120 --> 01:05:48,120
And the wild theories they'd concoct in order to explain

1383
01:05:48,120 --> 01:05:51,120
