1463
01:08:50,120 --> 01:08:51,120
No, my lord.

1464
01:08:51,120 --> 01:08:53,120
Our gods are always angry and give orders.

1465
01:08:53,120 --> 01:08:54,120
Oh, she's Catholic.

1466
01:08:54,120 --> 01:08:55,120
You smile.

1467
01:08:55,120 --> 01:08:58,120
If I ever get out of here,

1468
01:08:58,120 --> 01:09:00,120
into my world.

1469
01:09:00,120 --> 01:09:02,120
The world of light and flowers?

1470
01:09:03,120 --> 01:09:04,120
Will you come with me?

1471
01:09:04,120 --> 01:09:06,120
Yes, my lord.

1472
01:09:06,120 --> 01:09:08,120
My lord.

1473
01:09:08,120 --> 01:09:09,120
Can you zip me?

1474
01:09:09,120 --> 01:09:10,120
What is it?

1475
01:09:10,120 --> 01:09:11,120
The king wishes to see you at once.

1476
01:09:11,120 --> 01:09:13,120
He can't remember a line from Carousel.

1477
01:09:13,120 --> 01:09:18,120
Thanks for the bucket of cold water, Clorox face.

1478
01:09:18,120 --> 01:09:22,120
I should have cut this off a long time ago.

1479
01:09:22,120 --> 01:09:26,120
It's new in the hollow tree, you freaks.

1480
01:09:26,120 --> 01:09:29,120
The captain of the gods has been found murdered.

1481
01:09:29,120 --> 01:09:31,120
The beasts of the dark have done it.

1482
01:09:31,120 --> 01:09:33,120
It is possible they intend to revolt.

1483
01:09:33,120 --> 01:09:34,120
What about your guards?

1484
01:09:34,120 --> 01:09:35,120
Cowards.

1485
01:09:35,120 --> 01:09:36,120
Hey!

1486
01:09:36,120 --> 01:09:38,120
